  "notes": "Paper (Depta, Hufnagel, Schmidt-Hoberg, arXiv:2002.08370, JCAP 2020) derives robust BBN + Planck Neff constraints on ALPs coupled to photons in the keV-GeV mass range. Main results are presented graphically in the m_phi - tau_phi plane (figs. 4-6) and m_phi - g_phigamma plane (fig. 6 right); no numerical tables are provided. The data_points above are an APPROXIMATE upper boundary of the excluded region in the standard-cosmology scenario, reconstructed from text statements (exclusion of tau_phi >~ 0.1 s at large masses corresponding to the onset of BBN; sub-MeV ALPs excluded over essentially the full plotted coupling range because entropy transfer to photons after neutrino decoupling lowers Neff regardless of lifetime) and converted via tau = 64*pi/(m^3 g^2) with 1 s = 1.519e24 GeV^-1. Couplings BELOW the quoted boundary (longer lifetimes) are excluded down to very small g in the high-reheating-temperature scenario (down to the bottom of the plotted range ~1e-11 GeV^-1); this is a closed cosmological-triangle-type region, not a standard upper limit. Points should be replaced with a proper digitization of fig. 6 (right) for quantitative use. Weakened variants with extra Delta_Neff, neutrino chemical potential, or low reheating temperature are also given but the standard-scenario bound is reported here. Not a DM haloscope: no local DM density assumed. | vector-trace candidate: neff_opt_gphi.pdf colour (0.25, 0.41, 0.88), 165 pts (selected among 12) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 165))",
